  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 133 AM CST Thu Nov 19 2026\n\nA swath of moisture around 850mb will spread slowly northeast\nthrough the mid-section of the Quad State today. This moisture\nshould mix down to the surface in the afternoon, leading to \nincreased relative humidity compared to yesterday's 15-30%. \n\nOtherwise, with the relatively dry air in place, temperatures\nwill continue trend warmer with much of the region reaching the\nupper 60s today and the lower 70s Friday and Saturday.\nIncreasing clouds and humidity may hold temperatures down a bit\non Saturday, so Friday should be the warmest day. \n\nA cold front will pass Sunday afternoon and evening, and the\nlatest guidance has trended higher with PoPs during the day\nSunday with a 50-75% chance now forecast for the entire region.\nThis also comes with an increase in QPF which now ranges from a\ntenth to a quarter inch. The 00Z ECENS and GEFS support this\nincrease in QPF.\n\nThe cold front will pack quite a punch, with temperatures\ndropping a few degrees below normal for Monday's highs, and then\ndown into the 40s, or 5-10 degrees below normal, for Tuesday\nthrough Thanksgiving. Guidance continues to be non-committal for\nprecipitation mid to late next week, which results in an\neffectively dry forecast for now.",
